#: Game.lean:19
msgid "# Welcome to Vector Calculus in Lean\n"
"\n"
"### A Calculus III proof adventure\n"
"\n"
"Explore vectors, curves, multivariable derivatives, multiple integrals, and vector integral theorems across **16 worlds and 96 challenges**.\n"
"\n"
"## Start here\n"
"\n"
"Choose **Vector Workshop** on the world map, then open **Coordinates**. Each world has six levels; its final level brings the earlier ideas together.\n"
"\n"
"## Before you begin\n"
"\n"
"You should have completed the Natural Number Game and studied single-variable calculus. New calculus notation and a small set of additional tactics are explained where you need them.\n"
"\n"
"## Playing a level\n"
"\n"
"Read the objective, inspect the goal, and enter a tactic. The inventory explains the tools you have unlocked. Use the progressive hints when you need a nudge. **Regular** game rules enforce the unlock sequence.\n"
"\n"
"## The final worlds\n"
"\n"
"The integral-theorem challenges use explicitly stated, fully proved special cases. Each level tells you which result applies and what it establishes."
msgstr ""

#: Game.lean:21
msgid "## About this game\n"
"\n"
"Original vector-calculus exercises aligned with [OpenStax Calculus Volume 3](https://openstax.org/books/calculus-volume-3/pages/preface). Proofs use Lean 4 and Mathlib.\n"
"\n"
"## Mathematical scope\n"
"\n"
"The later worlds include proved special-case families for Green, Stokes, and Gauss, and verified coordinate-side integration examples. They are labeled as special cases rather than proofs of the general integral theorems.\n"
"\n"
"## Project and references\n"
"\n"
"[Game repository](https://github.com/andrewpringle/LEAN-Server-Vector-Calculus-Game) · [Lean4Game framework](https://github.com/leanprover-community/lean4game)\n"
"\n"
"The repository contains the curriculum map, source references, verification status, and full tactic-unlock schedule."
msgstr ""

