"\n"
"Mathematical prerequisites: Curl; positively oriented boundaries; parametrized surface flux. Earlier levels of Stokes Summit.\n"
"\n"
"Apply the proved Stokes special case for a shear field on the upward unit-square patch. The boundary is the counterclockwise square established earlier, and the field is smooth. §0 packages this verified family; it is not a general arbitrary-surface theorem.\n"
"\n"
"Exercise: prove the statement below."
msgstr ""

