"\n"
"Mathematical prerequisites: Partial derivatives; unit directions; chain rule and matrices. Earlier levels of Gradient Mountain.\n"
"\n"
"For the composite (t²)², evaluate the derivative of the outer square at the inner value t². Name the two scalar derivative facts. §0 multiplies them, and §1 lets you finish by proving the product equals the requested polynomial. This keeps the chain-rule choice separate from algebra. The named arguments §2 and §3 specify the outer and inner functions explicitly so Lean need not infer a function from one of its values.\n"
"\n"
"Exercise: prove the statement below."
msgstr ""

#. §0: `vector_ne_zero`
#: Game/Levels/SpaceExplorer/L06_BossThreePoints.lean:13
